          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Karoubi envelope
            or
            %em idempotent completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal
            enlargement of the category with the property that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} split idempotent
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %p
            A category in which all idempotents split is called
            %em Karoubi complete
            or
            %em Cauchy complete
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em idempotent-complete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            operation into such categories.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p There is an
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#AbstractDefinition"} Abstract definition
          %p
            that characterizes idempotent completions. In particular the idempotent completion always exists and is unique up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InComponents"} Construction in components
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#UnderTheYonedaEmbedding"} Construction via the Yoneda embedding
          %p
            For more constructions and equivalent characterizations see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+complete+category"} Cauchy complete category
            in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Cauchy+complete+category#InOrdinaryCategoryTheory"} In ordinary category theory
          %h3#AbstractDefinition Abstract definition
          #IdempotentCompletionAbstractly.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \tilde \mathcal{C}
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \mathcal{C}
              as an
              %strong idempotent completion
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi 𝒞
